## PR Title
Inline small CFuncs to reduce function call overhead

## PR Description
Adds two new command-line options - `--inline-cfuncs <n>` (default 20) and `--inline-cfuncs-product <n>` (default 200) - that let Verilator inline small CFunc calls directly into their callers, eliminating function-call overhead when `--output-split-cfuncs` puts callees in a separate translation unit that the C++ compiler cannot inline across.

Inlining criteria: function size <= n nodes (always inline), or size * call_count <= product threshold; the function must contain no `$c()` statements, return `void`, and be in the same scope as its callers. Local variables are cloned with unique names (`__Vinline_<func>_<var>`). The optimisation is automatically disabled by `--prof-cfuncs` or `--trace`.

This PR supersedes #6765, with the implementation moved out of `V3OrderCFuncEmitter` into a separate `V3InlineCFuncs` pass; `--inline-cfuncs` was changed from a boolean flag into a numeric threshold; variable merging was added; and `V3Stats` tracks "Optimizations, Inlined CFuncs". Coverage at merge: 100% line (80/80), 88.46% branches (46/52).

## PR Comments
The maintainer requested allowing inlining of functions with local variables (rather than excluding them) and suggested using two tunable thresholds for flexibility - the author implemented both. Multiple test cases were added to cover enabled/disabled states and threshold behavior. Merged on Dec 21, 2025.

